    {
      "id": "RPC-02",
      "chapter": "global",
      "title": "Four error contributions on a quotient of positive negative index",
      "anchor": "global-relative-error",
      "statement": "With U=n f log n, α=exp(−U/4), δ=exp(−n² f), the indefinite unitary count satisfies |D−M|≤(2α+δ)M+δD.",
      "hypotheses": "Fix A≥0 before choosing n₀. Assume uniform signature (p,q), q²≤n, n≥n₀(A), log rd≤exp(n), log f≤√n, b≥2, log b≤exp(U/16), |λ_{v,i}|≤b², 1≤g≤b^A, and a completely split auxiliary prime g₀>4n. The required opposite-sign spectral gap is at least 8·10^14(A+4)n^19 f^5 log(b rd). The tensor, Haar and admissible-projector data also enter. The indefinite branch requires q≥1; the definite q=0 branch invokes an exact count.",
      "definitions": [
        "U=n f log n, α=e^(−U/4) and δ=e^(−n²f).",
        "Moderate means least(x)≥(n f rd g b)^(−11q). Least(x) is the infimum of normalized sizes of nonzero sublattices. Deep is the complement in the fundamental domain.",
        "Near means a nonzero rational term satisfies the archimedean test at all places with epN=10^(−6)n^(−8)f^(−2). Only near nonidentity terms enter nearAbs."
      ],
